## 4. Merchant requirement-to-component matrix

Start with the merchant's business requirement rather than selecting a feature first.

| Merchant requirement | Relevant component | Key question |
|---|---|---|
| Group customers by service or billing relationship | Collection | How should customers be grouped? |
| Define a product or service | Plan | What is being sold? |
| Configure a fixed recurring price | Pricing | What amount and frequency apply? |
| Charge based on units or quantity | Pricing | Where does the quantity come from and who calculates it? |
| Offer different price tiers | Pricing | Which pricing model and calculation rules apply? |
| Publish an offer for customer purchase | Pricing Table | Where will customers discover and select the offer? |
| Register and identify customers | Member Center | What identifies a customer uniquely? |
| Display billing information to customers | Billing Portal | Which information and self-service actions are enabled? |
| Bill customers on a common calendar date | Account Billing | Who owns the billing calendar? |
| Renew a recurring service | Subscription Lifecycle | What defines the renewal event? |
| Collect recurring payments | Payment Management | Which authorized payment method is eligible? |
| Recover failed payments | Payment Management + Subscription Lifecycle | What is the retry and recovery policy? |
| Change an existing subscription | Subscription Lifecycle | Is the change native, API-driven, or merchant-managed? |
| Reconcile collected payments | Payment Management | How are payments mapped to billing records? |

