## 12. Merchant implementation workflow

Use this sequence as the default discovery and delivery checklist.

### Stage 1 — Discover

- Understand merchant business model.
- Identify customer types and billing relationships.
- Understand products and services.
- Identify pricing and billing frequency.
- Determine payment and authorization requirements.
- Understand customer experience expectations.

### Stage 2 — Design

- Select Collection and customer structure.
- Define Plans and Pricing.
- Select the billing model.
- Define the subscription lifecycle.
- Select the integration model.
- Design payment and recovery handling.
- Define customer-facing interfaces.

### Stage 3 — Validate

- Confirm product capability status.
- Confirm country and merchant eligibility.
- Validate API and webhook requirements.
- Validate payment-method support.
- Test billing and payment behavior.
- Confirm operational ownership.

### Stage 4 — Implement

- Configure the merchant solution.
- Integrate required systems.
- Configure customer journeys.
- Set up notifications and reporting.
- Prepare operational procedures.

### Stage 5 — Test and launch

- Run end-to-end scenarios.
- Validate financial reconciliation.
- Obtain merchant sign-off.
- Confirm support and escalation.
- Monitor the first billing cycles.

## 13. End-to-end test matrix

| Test area | Test scenario | Acceptance question |
|---|---|---|
| Customer | New customer registration | Is the correct customer record created or associated? |
| Collection | Customer assigned to a Collection | Is the correct relationship established? |
| Plan | Customer selects the intended service | Is the correct Plan applied? |
| Pricing | Price and frequency configured | Is the expected amount and schedule produced? |
| Pricing Table | Customer selects an offer | Does the journey lead to the intended checkout or registration flow? |
| Member Center | Customer identity is mapped | Is the identity association correct? |
| Subscription | Subscription is created | Are the intended terms recorded? |
| Billing | Billing event occurs | Is the correct amount due? |
| Account Billing | Calendar date is reached | Is the intended account billed? |
| Payment | Collection is initiated | Is the correct method and amount used? |
| Failure | Payment attempt fails | Is the failure handled correctly? |
| Recovery | Eligible failure is retried or resolved | Is recovery recorded correctly? |
| Portal | Customer reviews billing | Is the displayed information accurate? |
| Cancellation | Subscription is terminated | Are future billing actions handled correctly? |
| Reconciliation | Payment result is matched | Does the merchant record agree with the payment outcome? |

