## 16. Go-live readiness scorecard

Use this scorecard before approving a merchant launch.

| Readiness dimension | Required evidence | Status |
|---|---|---|
| Business model | Approved merchant use case | Not assessed |
| Product configuration | Collection, Plan, Pricing validated | Not assessed |
| Billing model | Account or subscription model approved | Not assessed |
| Customer identity | Customer mapping tested | Not assessed |
| Customer interface | Pricing Table, Member Center, Portal validated as applicable | Not assessed |
| Payment | Payment method and authorization tested | Not assessed |
| Failure handling | Retry and recovery policy approved | Not assessed |
| Integration | API, webhook, or hosted workflow tested | Not assessed |
| Reconciliation | Financial and billing matching tested | Not assessed |
| Country readiness | ID/MY scope confirmed | Not assessed |
| Operations | Support and escalation owners assigned | Not assessed |

Suggested approval rule:
- **Ready:** All critical items have evidence and owner sign-off.
- **Conditionally ready:** Remaining items have documented mitigation and explicit approval.
- **Not ready:** Critical payment, billing, customer identity, or reconciliation risks remain unresolved.

## 17. Product gap capture template

When a merchant requirement cannot be met, record it systematically.

| Field | Description |
|---|---|
| Gap ID | Unique tracking reference |
| Merchant / segment | Who needs the capability? |
| Country | ID, MY, or both |
| Business problem | What outcome is blocked? |
| Current workaround | How is it handled today? |
| Required capability | What must the product do? |
| Impact | Revenue, customer experience, operations, compliance |
| Frequency | One merchant or repeated market demand? |
| Priority | Business urgency and strategic value |
| Dependencies | Engineering, payment partner, legal, operations |
| Product decision | Gap, conditional support, or roadmap candidate |
| Owner | Accountable product owner |
| Target review | Next review or roadmap decision date |

Do not convert a merchant workaround into a claim that the platform natively supports the requested feature.

